This is an update to baseenv that only includes the newest and cleanest
codes. This include smptest (a newer version of nodecomm), a hardware
hierarchy query, and a routines for a Cartesian process topology (a
better MPI_Cart_create).

All (visible) routines have a prefix of either MPIX (for routines that require
MPI) or BENV (all others). To the extent possible, routines avoid requiring
the use of MPI so that they can be used in other contexts and tested without
a specific MPI environment.

Internal but still visible (i.e., not declared static) routines have prefix
MPIXi or BENVi.

Naming convention:
MPI-like routines, e.g., replacements for MPI_Cart_xxx, follow the same pattern,
using underscores between words. E.g., MPIX_Nodecart_create

Other routine use capital letters, e.g., BENV_HwdescGetDescGeneral
